@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Receiver cohort experiment
+
+This branch remains experimental. Defaults retain the previous allocator.
+The candidate uses the same configuration in every workload:
+
+```
+--guard_tail_congestion_gate 1 --guard_adaptive_fabric_target 1
+--guard_queue_budget_bdps 4 --guard_adaptive_target_max_bdps 8
+--guard_receiver_concurrency 1 --guard_concurrency_min_bdps 12
+--guard_scheduling_horizon_bdps 128
+```
+
+The receiver defines one service horizon using the largest active path BDP.
+When every competing message has more than that horizon remaining, it gives
+equal weights. When a short message is present, it retains inverse-remaining
+weights. Concurrent messages from one source retain their local remaining-size
+ordering for long transfers. Bounded messages from one source can receive
+ordered grants; this avoids spreading one sender's grant across short messages
+that compete for the same fabric path.
+
+The legacy K bound applies to a bounded receiver cohort. A mixed set with short
+messages outside the concurrency class retains weighted simultaneous service.
+Equal-size ties use a stable endpoint-and-flow hash. Any configured minimum
+share applies to deferred as well as selected flows, without exceeding receiver
+capacity. The horizon option is unsupported with the optional serialized vector
+allocator; the CLI rejects that combination.
+
+`--guard_fabric_control 0` disables only the fabric feedback component of GUARD.
+It retains ACK coalescing, sender scheduling, receiver grants and the fixed
+window. The older `guard-active-only` mode remains available, but also changes
+those sender/ACK behaviors, so it is not a single-component ablation.
+
+Behavioral allocator checks are in `tests/guard_scheduling_horizon.cc`.
+`tests/test_output_reservation.py` exercises a concurrent output-directory
+collision observed during development. The driver now reserves each directory
+atomically and retries a conflicting identifier without overwriting outputs.
+
+Development attempts, negative results, frozen confirmation manifests, input
+identities and raw archives live in
+`/home/gengjiayao/ict/work/guard_balanced_20260921`.
+No universal performance advantage is assumed. Promotion requires the complete
+confirmation results, including storage, DP2, fairness and matched ablations.
