--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/guard-scope-safety.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Scope-safety experiment, September 2026
+
+This branch evaluates an experimental profile. It does not change the default
+GUARD profile and does not establish superiority on every workload or metric.
+The fixed confirmation profile is:
+
+```text
+--guard_tail_congestion_gate 1
+--guard_adaptive_fabric_target 1
+--guard_queue_budget_bdps 4
+--guard_receiver_concurrency 1
+--guard_concurrency_min_bdps 12
+```
+
+All other parameters retain the defaults of source commit 17df579. In
+particular, lambda is 1.8, ACK spacing is eight packets, and the tail threshold
+is eight exact path BDPs. The profile is shared across workloads.
+
+The changes address three hypotheses:
+
+1. Guarded tail bypass continues processing INT. Eligibility can remain
+   latched, while the latest congestion samples revoke permission to bypass
+   the shared-fabric cap. An acknowledged prefix is required before entering
+   the guarded tail phase.
+2. Tail permission depends on queued work, rather than utilization divided by
+   a relaxed target above one. The safe threshold is the configured queue
+   budget times `guard_tail_safe_ratio`; the default ratio is 0.9. Feedback
+   delay can overshoot this threshold: it is not a hard queue bound.
+3. The legacy receiver scheduler applies its concurrency limit when multiple
+   source NICs compete. A single source already schedules its own messages;
+   duplicating that ordering at the receiver hurt the DP2 development trace.
+   This change applies to the legacy allocator and its counters. It does not
+   modify the optional serialized V14/V18 allocator.
+
+The original unguarded tail mode remains available for matched controls.
+HPCC, Homa, DCQCN, and TIMELY receive no algorithm changes. The experiment
+records all configurations, input hashes, shared-library hashes, and completed
+flow identities. Development uses seed 301; independent confirmation freezes
+seeds 401–405 before outcomes are inspected. Rejected configurations, runtime
+errors, and adverse results remain in the evidence directory.
+
+Evidence and runners:
+`/home/gengjiayao/ict/work/guard_optimization_20260921`.
+The confirmation manifest records the exact tested source commit; this
+documentation may be committed after that freeze without changing the tested
+implementation. A broad release requires reviewing the storage, DP2, and
+fairness regressions, not merely the Ring loss improvement.
